ling or outside spending shifts in the final weeks, especially if DiLorenzo's Trump-distance message gains traction with independents.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Chris Pappas (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Chris Pappas is leaving the seat to run for Senate, making this an open contest in a district that only leans two points Democratic. Stefany Shaheen, daughter of the state's former senator, survived a tight primary and enters with a cash advantage and roughly $2.2 million in outside support from Democratic groups. Republican Anthony DiLorenzo, who has raised about $2.5 million largely self-funded, is running as a moderate who breaks with Trump on tariffs and tone.\n\nA late-September University of New Hampshire poll shows Shaheen up four points among likely voters, and prediction markets put her chances near 92%. Expert ratings range from Lean D to Safe D, with a consensus around Likely D. The race is competitive but tilts clearly toward Democrats.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.937, "margin": 10.01}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9238, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9245, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8928, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8695, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.844, "margin": 7.0}]}